{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-05T06:11:09.907Z","author":"pi-glm","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"pi","agent_model":"glm-5.3:cloud","agent_model_source":"environment","agent_instance":"532a978510ffac27394c1e6c","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"glm-5.3:cloud","source":"environment"},"effort":null,"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null},"op":"update","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-05T06:11:09.907Z"},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/status","value":"in_progress"}],"before_hash":"35d067343149f57e9468f3602ce1370cd8647bad4ace8cc3d56bc5c4c600a80c","after_hash":"57894729632020de59bdb510f8bb7cafb9b8009189f1f5a96f658b5eb6fa7a34","item_hash_version":3,"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"d88319c53d49107ced6b81cb131a9674c2d88bf46e357dc942253fb020ed06c0"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-05T06:14:06.813Z","author":"pi-glm","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"pi","agent_model":"glm-5.3:cloud","agent_model_source":"environment","agent_instance":"532a978510ffac27394c1e6c","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"glm-5.3:cloud","source":"environment"},"effort":null,"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/2","value":{"created_at":"2026-10-05T06:14:06.813Z","author":"pi-glm","text":"Design for the served repository, reusing engine/transport.ts rather than forking it. The Transport interface stays the single boundary: its methods become async (a wire is asynchronous, a filesystem is not, and the interface was written so the algorithm does not care), FileTransport keeps every policy - fast-forward, force, compare-and-swap publication, verified arrival - and the HTTP server delegates every repository operation to a FileTransport opened on the repository directory under --root. Wire: POST <base>/advertise|fetch|push|objects/missing|objects/upload|publish, JSON envelopes with base64 payloads, error body {code,message} mapped back to ObjectStoreError so refusals read identically to a file remote. Client: HttpTransport implements the same interface, so clone/fetch/push/remote-add work unchanged through openTransport; the bearer token travels in the remote URL's userinfo. Resumable uploads keep their connection identity: the server holds one FileTransport per upload session, so publish reports exactly what that session delivered. Series and review records ride the same object paths: records are tree-reachable, series objects transfer through the verified-arrival upload path. Tenancy: bearer tokens scoped per repository (read/write); every pre-authorization failure - missing repo, wrong tenant, bad token, path traversal - answers with one byte-identical 404 denial; body sizes, object counts and session counts are bounded."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-05T06:14:06.813Z"}],"before_hash":"57894729632020de59bdb510f8bb7cafb9b8009189f1f5a96f658b5eb6fa7a34","after_hash":"8c6a1c7849e8df86d91d487f633b78b7d1106ce03c230f456033cd2471df1947","item_hash_version":3,"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"8da4ec711d81ca922dcdbfc75aa3b9d99476e68b862daa3833813191ed7b7d73"}
